<MECA ID = "T010251A387A239" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Apr2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Idle Speed Control</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The engine control computer controls the throttle valve opening to the optimum position to maintain the target idle speed under various conditions.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<INDICATE ID = "T010251A387A239I01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Idle Speed Control List</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "19%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "80%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Starting Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>When the engine is started, the throttle valve is opened to increase the intake air volume and improve engine startability.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" MOREROWS = "4" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Predictive Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>When the signals below are detected, the throttle valve opening is controlled to suppress speed fluctuations.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When a change in idle speed is predicted.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When the electrical load changes.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When the A/C switch is operated.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When the shift position is changed.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Deceleration Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>During deceleration, the throttle valve is opened to increase the intake air flow, lowering the vacuum in the intake manifold, which reduces the consumption of oil drawn into the combustion chamber, prevents engine stall due to a sudden drop in engine speed and improves driveability.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Feedback Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>The engine speed is measured for a certain period, and if there is a difference from the target speed, the throttle valve opening is controlled to bring the idle speed to the target value.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></INDICATE>
<SPEC ID = "T010251A387A239X02" INDSW = "OFF">
